.TH "SVGGRAPHICSELEMENT.GETBBOX" "3JS" "September 14, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGGraphicsElement.getBBox \- SVGGraphicsElement: getBBox() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]getBBox()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]SVGGraphicsElement\f[R] interface returns the smallest rectangle
that contains the element.
The rectangle is measured in the user coordinate system of the element,
with the geometry attributes of the element and its descendants applied.
.PP
By default, the rectangle covers only the shape of the element.
The \f[CR]options\f[R] parameter lets you include the stroke and the
markers as well, and limit the rectangle to the part of the element that
its clipping path leaves visible.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]getBBox()\f[R] returns the bounding box as it is
at the time of the call, even if the element hasn\(cqt been rendered
yet.
It also doesn\(cqt account for any transformation applied to the element
or its parents.
.RE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]getBBox()\f[R] returns different values than
\f[CR]getBoundingClientRect()\f[R], because the latter returns values
relative to the viewport.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getBBox()
getBBox(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object that controls which parts of the element are included in the
bounding box.
It can have the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]fill\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value indicating whether the shape of the element is included
in the bounding box.
Defaults to \f[CR]true\f[R].
The shape is included even when the element has no fill, so an element
with \f[CR]fill\f[R] set to \f[CR]none\f[R] still contributes to the
bounding box.
.TP
\f[B]stroke\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value indicating whether the stroke of the element is included
in the bounding box, together with its line caps and line joins.
Defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
It has no effect when the \f[CR]stroke\f[R] property is \f[CR]none\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]markers\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value indicating whether the markers of the element are
included in the bounding box.
Defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
Each marker contributes the shapes drawn inside it, rather than the
entire area defined by its \f[CR]markerWidth\f[R] and
\f[CR]markerHeight\f[R] attributes.
.TP
\f[B]clipped\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value indicating whether the bounding box is limited to the
part of the element that its \f[CR]clip\-path\f[R] leaves visible.
Defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]DOMRect\f[R] object describing the bounding box in the user
coordinate system of the element, regardless of any transformation
applied to the element or its parents.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] Browsers currently return an \f[CR]SVGRect\f[R] object
defined in SVG 1.1, which has the same \f[CR]x\f[R], \f[CR]y\f[R],
\f[CR]width\f[R], and \f[CR]height\f[R] properties, but isn\(cqt a
\f[CR]DOMRect\f[R] instance.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Comparing bounding boxes
This example outlines the same \f[CR]<g>\f[R] element twice.
The green outline is an SVG \f[CR]<rect>\f[R] placed with the rectangle
returned by \f[CR]getBBox()\f[R], and the red one is an absolutely
positioned \f[CR]<div>\f[R] placed with the rectangle returned by
\f[CR]getBoundingClientRect()\f[R].
Both outlines cover the same text, but the values below them differ:
\f[CR]getBBox()\f[R] reports user units, while
\f[CR]getBoundingClientRect()\f[R] reports CSS pixels relative to the
viewport.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 200 60\(dq xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq>
  <\f[B]g\f[R] id=\(dqgreeting\(dq>
    <\f[B]text\f[R] x=\(dq5\(dq y=\(dq16\(dq transform=\(dqscale(2, 2)\(dq>Hello World!</\f[B]text\f[R]>
    <\f[B]text\f[R] x=\(dq8\(dq y=\(dq32\(dq transform=\(dqtranslate(0 20) scale(1.25 1)\(dq>
      Hello World Again!
    </\f[B]text\f[R]>
  </\f[B]g\f[R]>
  <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqbbox\(dq stroke=\(dqgreen\(dq stroke\-width=\(dq2\(dq fill=\(dqnone\(dq />
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>

<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqclient\-rect\(dq></\f[B]div\f[R]>
<\f[B]ul\f[R] id=\(dqlegend\(dq></\f[B]ul\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
svg {
  \f[B]max\-width\f[R]: 400px;
}

client\-rect {
  \f[B]position\f[R]: absolute;
  \f[B]box\-sizing\f[R]: border\-box;
  \f[B]border\f[R]: 2px dashed red;
}

ul {
  \f[B]padding\-inline\-start\f[R]: 1em;
  \f[B]font\-family\f[R]: monospace;
  \f[B]line\-height\f[R]: 1.5;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] greeting = document.querySelector(\(dq#greeting\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] legend = document.querySelector(\(dq#legend\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] bbox = greeting.getBBox();
\f[B]const\f[R] outline = document.querySelector(\(dq#bbox\(dq);
outline.setAttribute(\(dqx\(dq, bbox.x);
outline.setAttribute(\(dqy\(dq, bbox.y);
outline.setAttribute(\(dqwidth\(dq, bbox.width);
outline.setAttribute(\(dqheight\(dq, bbox.height);

\f[B]const\f[R] clientRect = greeting.getBoundingClientRect();
\f[B]const\f[R] overlay = document.querySelector(\(dq#client\-rect\(dq);
overlay.style.left = \(ga${clientRect.x + window.scrollX}px\(ga;
overlay.style.top = \(ga${clientRect.y + window.scrollY}px\(ga;
overlay.style.width = \(ga${clientRect.width}px\(ga;
overlay.style.height = \(ga${clientRect.height}px\(ga;

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] [label, rect] \f[B]of\f[R] [
  [\(dqgetBBox()\(dq, bbox],
  [\(dqgetBoundingClientRect()\(dq, clientRect],
]) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] item = document.createElement(\(dqli\(dq);
  item.textContent = \(ga${label} → ${rect.x.toFixed(1)}, ${rect.y.toFixed(1)}, ${rect.width.toFixed(1)}, ${rect.height.toFixed(1)}\(ga;
  legend.append(item);
}
.EE
.SS Result
.SS Bounding box options
This example draws a path with a thick stroke, a marker at each end, and
a clipping path.
Each call to \f[CR]getBBox()\f[R] turns on one more option, and each
resulting rectangle is outlined in a different color: the shape alone in
red, the stroke added in green, the markers added in orange, and the
result clipped in black.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] viewBox=\(dq0 0 200 150\(dq xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq>
  <\f[B]defs\f[R]>
    <\f[B]marker\f[R]
      id=\(dqdot\(dq
      viewBox=\(dq0 0 10 10\(dq
      refX=\(dq5\(dq
      refY=\(dq5\(dq
      markerUnits=\(dquserSpaceOnUse\(dq
      markerWidth=\(dq30\(dq
      markerHeight=\(dq30\(dq>
      <\f[B]circle\f[R] cx=\(dq5\(dq cy=\(dq5\(dq r=\(dq5\(dq fill=\(dqrebeccapurple\(dq />
    </\f[B]marker\f[R]>
    <\f[B]clipPath\f[R] id=\(dqclip\(dq>
      <\f[B]rect\f[R] x=\(dq40\(dq y=\(dq40\(dq width=\(dq120\(dq height=\(dq80\(dq />
    </\f[B]clipPath\f[R]>
  </\f[B]defs\f[R]>

  <\f[B]path\f[R]
    id=\(dqchevron\(dq
    d=\(dqM 50 100 L 100 50 L 150 100\(dq
    fill=\(dqnone\(dq
    stroke=\(dqcornflowerblue\(dq
    stroke\-width=\(dq20\(dq
    marker\-start=\(dqurl(#dot)\(dq
    marker\-end=\(dqurl(#dot)\(dq
    clip\-path=\(dqurl(#clip)\(dq />

  <\f[B]g\f[R] fill=\(dqnone\(dq stroke\-width=\(dq1\(dq>
    <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqfill\-box\(dq stroke=\(dqred\(dq />
    <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqstroke\-box\(dq stroke=\(dqgreen\(dq />
    <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqmarkers\-box\(dq stroke=\(dqorange\(dq />
    <\f[B]rect\f[R] id=\(dqclipped\-box\(dq stroke=\(dqblack\(dq />
  </\f[B]g\f[R]>
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>

<\f[B]ul\f[R] id=\(dqlegend\(dq></\f[B]ul\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
.IP
.EX
svg {
  \f[B]max\-width\f[R]: 400px;
}

ul {
  \f[B]padding\-inline\-start\f[R]: 1em;
  \f[B]font\-family\f[R]: monospace;
  \f[B]line\-height\f[R]: 1.5;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] chevron = document.querySelector(\(dq#chevron\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] legend = document.querySelector(\(dq#legend\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] variants = [
  { id: \(dqfill\-box\(dq, label: \(dqgetBBox()\(dq, options: {} },
  {
    id: \(dqstroke\-box\(dq,
    label: \(dqgetBBox({ stroke: true })\(dq,
    options: { stroke: \f[B]true\f[R] },
  },
  {
    id: \(dqmarkers\-box\(dq,
    label: \(dqgetBBox({ stroke: true, markers: true })\(dq,
    options: { stroke: \f[B]true\f[R], markers: \f[B]true\f[R] },
  },
  {
    id: \(dqclipped\-box\(dq,
    label: \(dqgetBBox({ stroke: true, markers: true, clipped: true })\(dq,
    options: { stroke: \f[B]true\f[R], markers: \f[B]true\f[R], clipped: \f[B]true\f[R] },
  },
];

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] { id, label, options } \f[B]of\f[R] variants) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] box = chevron.getBBox(options);

  \f[B]const\f[R] outline = document.querySelector(\(ga#${id}\(ga);
  outline.setAttribute(\(dqx\(dq, box.x);
  outline.setAttribute(\(dqy\(dq, box.y);
  outline.setAttribute(\(dqwidth\(dq, box.width);
  outline.setAttribute(\(dqheight\(dq, box.height);

  \f[B]const\f[R] item = document.createElement(\(dqli\(dq);
  item.style.color = outline.getAttribute(\(dqstroke\(dq);
  item.textContent = \(ga${label} → ${box.x.toFixed(1)}, ${box.y.toFixed(1)}, ${box.width.toFixed(1)}, ${box.height.toFixed(1)}\(ga;
  legend.append(item);
}
.EE
